 34CL c  1972Vi04: a 40-MeV proton beam was produced from the Grenoble          
 34CL2c  variable-energy cyclotron. The target was chlorine gas of natural      
 34CL3c  isotopic abundance. Deuterons were detected using a silicon telescope  
 34CL4c  consisted of a 500-|mm surface barrier |DE detector, a 3-mm            
 34CL5c  lithium-drifted silicon E detector, and another 3-mm lithium-drifted   
 34CL6c  silicon E detector in anti-coincidence (FWHM=85 keV). Measured         
 34CL7c  |s(E{-d},|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, L-transfers, and spectroscopic    
 34CL8c  factors from DWUCK-DWBA analysis of the measured |s(|q).               
 34CL cL $Spectroscopic factor of is obtained by:                               
 34CL2cL |s(|q){-exp}=1.53[(2s{-d}+1)/(2s{-p}+1)][(2s{-n}+1)/(2(2L+1))]         
